"Owen" <xe2vske02@sneakemail.com> writes:
> I was playing slashem, and was blinded carrying a corpse into the
> co-aligned minetown temple. I thought this would be no problem - move
> with 'm', to make sure I don't attack the priest, and I'll be safe.
> However, he still got angry, and killed me. I thought it was odd that
> slashem was different than Nethack in this regard, so wizmode checked
> in nethack - exactly the same. Is my understanding of the 'm' move
> command completely wrong, then?

'm' will only refrain from attacking a monster if you have reason to
believe one is there; seen, a remembered 'I', warning, etc. If you
move into an _unknown_ unseen monster's square with 'm', you'll
blunder into it with no great effect other than angering it if it's
peaceful. In your circumstances, you want to be searching ahead of you
before moving.

